B build minutes)\\\\n   • Sanity Free = $0 (see limits above)\\\\n   • Domain ≈ $12/yr (Namecheap / Route 53)\\\\n   • Optional upgrades: Vercel Pro $20/mo if traffic grows; Sanity Growth $15/mo if user count or bandwidth grows.\\\\n\\\\n5. Security & Compliance\\\\n   • HTTPS everywhere (Vercel auto-provisioned certs)\\\\n   • CMS: RBAC; 2FA support\\\\n   • Content requests served via edge CDN, no direct DB exposure\\\\n   • Secrets (webhook tokens, revalidate keys) stored in Vercel & Sanity encrypted env vars\\\\n\\\\n6. Coordination Points for Other Directors\\\\n   • Backend Dir: Define /api/revalidate endpoint signature & any additional APIs (e.g., authenticated resident portal) using Next.js serverless or separate micro-service.\\\\n   • Frontend Dir: Adopt component library & content fetch hooks (Sanity client, or GraphQL if they prefer). Follow the above content schema; we can evolve schemas via migration scripts checked into repo.\\\\n\\\\n7. Alternative (in case requirements change)\\\\n   • Self-hosted Strapi on Render.com – open-source, Node-based, quick spin-up; slightly higher ops cost, but full data ownership.\\\\n   • Git-based Netlify CMS if budget must be $0 and editors comfortable using Git PR previews (less friendly for truly non-technical users, so kept as fallback).\\\\n\\\\n8. Next Steps (if plan approved)\\\\n   1) Initialize mono-repo (frontend + Sanity Studio) on GitHub.\\\\n   2) Configure Vercel project & environment variables.\\\\n   3) Scaffold Sanity Studio with schemas above; invite editors.\\\\n   4) Build News & Events pages with ISR and live preview.\\\\n   5) Document editor guide (1-page PDF / video GIF).\\\"\\n}\\n###<store-ops-plan-01>###\\n###<store-be-plan-01>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"Director Lystra's Initial Backend Architecture Plan (BE-PLAN-01):\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Guiding Principles\\\\n• Security-first: encryption in transit & at rest, OWASP Top-10 mitigations, least-privilege RBAC.\\\\n• Modular, test-driven, container-ready, horizontally scalable.\\\\n• Developer-friendly (TypeScript), clear API contract for the frontend team.\\\\n\\\\n2. Chosen Tech Stack (aligned with Ops Director’s preference for JS-centric stack)\\\\n• Runtime  : Node.js 20 + TypeScript\\\\n• Web FW   : Express 4 (with express-async-errors) or Fastify (pluggable, faster) – defaulting to Fastify unless Ops objects.\\\\n• ORM      : Prisma 5 (PostgreSQL adapter) to keep SQL transparent but typed.\\\\n• DB       : PostgreSQL 15 on AWS RDS (or CloudSQL/AzurePG; local via Docker).\\\\n• Auth     : JSON Web Tokens (short-lived Access, long-lived Refresh) + BCrypt-salted hashes; optional social login add-ons later.\\\\n• Queue    : Lightweight BullMQ/Redis for email dispatch so web thread stays cold-path.\\\\n• Email    : AWS SES (or SendGrid) via signed SMTP creds.\\\\n• Container: Docker; Prod orchestrated via ECS Fargate or Kubernetes cluster managed by Ops.\\\\n• Observab.: Pino logger → Loki/Grafana; metrics via Prom-compatible exporter.\\\\n\\\\n3. Database Schema (simplified ER diagram)\\\\n• users\\\\n  – id (PK, UUID)\\\\n  – email (unique, indexed)\\\\n  – password_hash\\\\n  – full_name\\\\n  – unit_number (varchar)   // apt / house identifier\\\\n  – phone (nullable)\\\\n  – is_email_verified (bool)\\\\n  – created_at, updated_at\\\\n\\\\n• roles (seed table)\\\\n  – id (PK)  e.g. RESIDENT, BOARD_MEMBER, ADMIN\\\\n\\\\n• user_roles (user_id FK → users, role_id FK → roles)\\\\n\\\\n• refresh_tokens\\\\n  – id (PK, UUID)\\\\n  – user_id FK\\\\n  – token_hash (sha256)\\\\n  – revoked (bool), expires_at, created_at, created_by_ip\\\\n\\\\n• announcements\\\\n  – id (PK, UUID)\\\\n  – title, body(markdown|html), published_at, author_id FK → users\\\\n\\\\n• documents\\\\n  – id (PK, UUID)\\\\n  – file_path (S3 URL), label, visibility (public | resident | board)\\\\n  – uploaded_by FK → users, uploaded_at\\\\n\\\\n• contact_messages\\\\n  – id (PK, UUID)\\\\n  – name, email, subject, message_text\\\\n  – status (NEW | IN_REVIEW | CLOSED)\\\\n  – received_at, handled_by FK → users\\\\n\\\\n(Prisma schema & migration scripts will be generated.)\\\\n\\\\n4. API Design (REST, versioned under /api/v1)\\\\n─ Auth\\\\n  • POST  /auth/register             → create resident account, send verify-email job\\\\n  • POST  /auth/login                → returns {access, refresh}\\\\n  • POST  /auth/refresh              → rotates refresh token\\\\n  • POST  /auth/logout               → revoke refresh token\\\\n  • POST  /auth/forgot-password\\\\\\\\n  • POST  /auth/reset-password\\\\\\\\n\\\\n─ Users (protected, role-based)\\\\n  • GET   /users/me                  → current profile\\\\n  • PATCH /users/me                  → update profile fields\\\\n  • GET   /users/:id                 → ADMIN/BOARD only\\\\n  • GET   /users?role=BOARD_MEMBER   → list board members\\\\n\\\\n─ Announcements\\\\n  • GET   /announcements             → public/resident filtered by role\\\\n  • POST  /announcements             → BOARD/ADMIN (create)\\\\n  • PATCH /announcements/:id         → author or ADMIN\\\\n  • DELETE/announcements/:id         → ADMIN\\\\n\\\\n─ Documents\\\\n  • GET   /documents?visibility=...  → returns presigned S3 URLs\\\\n  • POST  /documents (multipart)     → BOARD/ADMIN (uploads via signed URL flow)\\\\n\\\\n─ Contact Us\\\\n  • POST  /contact                   → anonymous or authenticated; body {name,email,subject,message}\\\\\\\\n  • GET   /contact/:id               → ADMIN only to view & change status\\\\n\\\\nAll endpoints follow RFC 7807 error object, 429 for rate-limit, express-validator for payloads.\\\\n\\\\n5. Authentication & Security Controls\\\\n• Password: 12+ chars, complexity rules, bcrypt-12 rounds.\\\\n• JWT Access: 15 min exp, signed w/ RS256 private key; kid rotation.\\\\n• Refresh token: 30 d lifetime, stored hashed in DB; rotate on every use (token theft detection).\\\\n• Email-verification & password-reset tokens stored hashed, expire 24 h.\\\\n• Middleware stack: helmet(), cors(allowedOrigins env), rateLimiter (redis-backing), csrf() for cookie-based flows.\\\\n• RBAC Guard: decorator or middleware mapping route → roles.\\\\n• Secrets via AWS Secrets Manager / Kubernetes Secrets; never baked into image.\\\\n• Automated SCA & SAST in CI (GitHub Actions).\\\\n\\\\n6. Contact Us Logic Flow\\\\n1. Client calls POST /contact.\\\\n2. Server validates & rate-limits (max 5/hr/IP).\\\\n3. Persist contact_messages row (status=NEW).\\\\n4. Queue job ‘email:contact’ with message ID.\\\\n5. Worker pulls job → formats email → SES send to designated board address.\\\\n6. Board/ops can view & mark status via ADMIN dashboard API.\\\\n\\\\n7. Testing Strategy\\\\n• Unit tests: Jest + supertest (service & controller layers)\\\\n• Integration: testcontainers spinning PostgreSQL & Redis.\\\\n• E2E smoke: simple k6 script hitting staging endpoints.\\\\n\\\\n8. Deployment Pipeline Sketch\\\\nGitHub → Actions\\\\n  – install, lint, test\\\\n  – build Docker image\\\\n  – push to ECR / GHCR\\\\n  – trigger staging deploy (Terraform plan-apply or Helm upgrade)\\\\n  – seed migrations via prisma migrate\\\\n  – promote to prod via manual approval.\\\\n\\\\n9. Work Breakdown (next steps)\\\\nA. Recruit Supervisor-level leads:\\\\n   • API/Service Lead – owns Fastify services & tests.\\\\n   • Auth Lead – builds the JWT/Refresh & RBAC modules.\\\\n   • DB Lead – finalizes Prisma schema & migrations.\\\\n   • Ops Integration Lead – scripts CI/CD & Terraform hand-off with Ops Director.\\\\nB. Each lead will spawn Attendants for individual files/components.\\\\nC. Produce detailed DEP specifying container build, secrets injection, environment matrix.\\\\nD. Submit DEP to Partagaz D for review, then request phase shift to Execution.\\\\n\\\\n10. Open Items / Alignment Needed\\\\n• Confirm Fastify vs Express preference.\\\\n• Domain for email (SES verified?) and SMTP provider selection.\\\\n• Whether social login (Google) is desired MVP.\\\\n• Logging/monitoring stack preference (ELK vs Loki).\\\"\\n}\\n###<store-be-plan-01>###\\n###<store-fe-plan-01>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"Director Jung's Initial Frontend Plan (FE-PLAN-01):\\\\n\\\\n──────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Guiding Principles\\\\n• Simplicity & Clarity: Clean layouts, limited color palette reflecting HOA branding, ample white-space.\\\\n• ‘Three-click’ navigation rule: Any public page reachable in ≤ 3 clicks.\\\\n• Responsive & Accessible: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance; mobile-first breakpoints (375 px, 768 px, 1280 px).\\\\n\\\\n2. Recommended Tech Stack\\\\n• Framework: Next.js (React 18 + App Router) with TypeScript – SEO-friendly, file-based routing, fast static builds, easy SSR/ISR when needed.\\\\n• Styling: Tailwind CSS (JIT) + twin.macro for conditional class merging; custom theme file for HOA colors, font scale, and spacing.\\\\n• UI Helpers: Headless UI (for accessible menus, dialogs) + Heroicons.\\\\n• State/Data: SWR (stale-while-revalidate) for lightweight data fetching + React Context for Auth. Easily swapped for React Query if Ops prefers.\\\\n• Auth Guard: Next.js Middleware to gate “/member/*” routes; expects a JWT in Http-only cookie issued by backend chosen by Ops.\\\\n• Tooling: ESLint, Prettier, Husky + lint-staged, Jest/React-Testing-Library & Playwright for e2e.\\\\n\\\\n3. Global Layout Components\\\\n• <MainLayout>: sticky header, dynamic nav, footer.\\\\n    Header: HOA logo (linked to “/”), primary nav links, Login/Logout button.\\\\n    Mobile: hamburger → slide-in menu (Headless UI <Dialog>). \\\\\\\\n• <AuthProvider>: wraps app, provides user & role context.\\\\n• <ProtectedRoute>: client-side fallback check (in addition to server middleware) to redirect unauth users.\\\\n\\\\n4. Page-Specific High-Level Wireframes / Descriptions\\\\nA. Public Pages\\\\n────────────────\\\\\\\\n1) Contact Us (/contact)\\\\n   • Hero banner with page title & tagline.\\\\n   • Two-column grid on desktop ⇢ single-column on mobile.\\\\n      Left: HOA office address, phone, email, Google Map iframe.\\\\n      Right: Contact form (Name, Email, Subject, Message) → POST /api/contact.\\\\n   • “Office Hours” info block & quick-links (FAQs, Dues).\\\\n\\\\n2) Bylaws (/bylaws)\\\\n   • Split-pane: sticky vertical Table-of-Contents sidebar (Article I-X) + content pane.\\\\n   • Each article in an <Accordion> allowing expand/collapse.\\\\n   • Search bar (client-side fuzzy search) scrolling to matches.\\\\n   • Download PDF button top-right.\\\\n\\\\n3) Schools (/schools)\\\\n   • Map banner (Leaflet or Google Maps) highlighting HOA boundary.\\\\n   • Filter chips: Elementary | Middle | High | Private.\\\\n   • Responsive grid of <SchoolCard>: name, type, distance, “More Info” link.\\\\n   • Optional accordion per district with embedded external links.\\\\n\\\\nB. Protected (Members-Only) Pages – all live under /member/*\\\\\\\\n──────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1) Dues (/member/dues)\\\\n   • Summary card: Current balance, last payment date, Next due date.\\\\n   • Payment CTA: “Pay Now” → modal w/ Stripe Checkout widget.\\\\n   • History table: Date | Amount | Method | Receipt download.\\\\n\\\\n2) Annual Meetings (/member/meetings)\\\\n   • Upcoming Meetings section: date, agenda, RSVP button.\\\\n   • Past Meetings accordion: Year headers → list of minutes (PDF) & recordings.\\\\n   • Reminder toggle (hooks into backend notifications).\\\\n\\\\n3) News & Events (/member/news-events)\\\\n   • Tabbed view: “News Feed” | “Events Calendar”.\\\\n   • News Feed: card list w/ thumbnail, headline, 2-line summary; link to full article page.\\\\n   • Events Calendar: Month view (FullCalendar) + agenda list for small screens.\\\\n   • Quick-add to Google/Apple via .ics links.\\\\n\\\\n5. Styling Strategy\\\\n• Tailwind theme config file (tailwind.config.ts):\\\\n  colors: primary #14426B, secondary #4BA3D3, neutral slate-variants.\\\\n  fontFamily: { sans: [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Inter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Helvetica\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sans-serif\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] }.\\\\n  extend spacing/typography scale to match Figma grid (8-pt system).\\\\n• Component-level composition via utility classes; extract frequently reused pieces (<Card>, <Button>, <Input>) into /components/ui/* for consistency.\\\\n• Use CSS Variables for theming; ready for dark-mode toggle.\\\\n\\\\n6. Navigation & Routing Map\\\\n/\\\\\\\\n├── contact\\\\\\\\n├── bylaws\\\\\\\\n├── schools\\\\\\\\n└── member\\\\\\\\n    ├── dues\\\\\\\\n    ├── meetings\\\\\\\\n    └── news-events\\\\\\\\n\\\\n7. Accessibility & UX Guarantees\\\\n• All interactive elements reachable by keyboard; focus outline visible.\\\\n• aria-labels on icons & form inputs; color contrast ≥ 4.5:1.\\\\n• prefers-reduced-motion respected for animations.\\\\n\\\\n8. Responsive Breakpoints Preview (representative)\\\\n• Mobile (<640 px): stacked layout, hamburger nav.\\\\n• Tablet (641-1023 px): grid-2 columns, collapsible sidebar.\\\\n• Desktop (≥1024 px): full multi-column, sticky TOC.\\\\n\\\\n9. Integration Notes for Ops Team\\\\n• Next.js front can be deployed on Vercel (edge-optimized) or containerized w/ Docker; environment vars NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_KEY etc. tie into backend endpoints.\\\\n• Auth middleware expects backend route /api/auth/refresh to validate and refresh JWT.\\\\n• SWR’s fetcher points to (process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL + endpoint).\\\\n\\\\n10. Estimated File/Component Breakdown (organised by feature folder)\\\\n  /components\\\\\\\\n    /ui (Button.tsx, Card.tsx, Input.tsx, Modal.tsx, etc.)\\\\\\\\n  /layouts/MainLayout.tsx\\\\\\\\n  /pages\\\\\\\\n    contact.tsx\\\\\\\\n    bylaws.tsx\\\\\\\\n    schools.tsx\\\\\\\\n    /member/dues.tsx\\\\\\\\n    /member/meetings.tsx\\\\\\\\n    /member/news-events.tsx\\\\\\\\n  /lib (auth.ts, fetcher.ts)\\\\\\\\n  /styles (globals.css, tailwind.css)\\\\\\\\n  /tests (unit & e2e)\\\\\\\\n\\\\n11. Next Steps / Suggestions\\\\n• Obtain logo/brand assets & any brand guidelines.\\\\n• Confirm backend auth + payment provider selections.\\\\n• Decide if server components (Next 13/14) or classic pages.\\\\n• Finalize content (bylaws text, school list, meeting PDFs) to wire into CMS or markdown repo.\\\"\\n}\\n###<store-fe-plan-01>###\\n###<OPS-PLAN-02>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Lagret, your proposed plan is excellent and is approved as the primary strategy. The use of Next.js, Vercel, and Sanity.io perfectly addresses the core requirements. \\\\n\\\\nYour next actions are:\\\\n1.  Establish the monorepo structure on GitHub.\\\\n2.  Set up the Sanity.io project with the initial schemas for 'newsArticle' and 'event'. Also include a schema for the 'Bylaws' page content to allow for easy updates.\\\\n3.  Set up the Vercel project linked to the repository.\\\\n4.  Securely share the Sanity Project ID, dataset name, and an API token with the Frontend Director. Share the Vercel project details with both the Frontend and Backend Directors.\\\\n5.  Collaborate with the Backend Director to finalize the hosting solution for their dedicated service (e.g., Vercel Serverless Functions for simple APIs, or a separate service on Render/AWS for the main database-heavy backend). \\\\n\\\\nReport back when these foundational steps are complete.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"OPS-PLAN-02\\\"\\n}\\n###<OPS-PLAN-02>###\\n###<BE-PLAN-02>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Lystra, your plan for the backend is robust, secure, and well-designed. It is approved with one key clarification: The responsibility for user-editable page content ('News', 'Events', 'Bylaws') will be handled by the Sanity.io CMS managed by the Ops Director. \\\\n\\\\nYour revised scope is:\\\\n1.  **User Management & Auth:** Implement the full user and roles system (PostgreSQL, Prisma) and the JWT authentication flow as you designed. This is your highest priority.\\\\n2.  **Secure File Management:** Implement the `documents` schema and API. This will be used for uploading and retrieving sensitive files like meeting minutes and financial reports, delivered to the frontend via secure, pre-signed URLs.\\\\n3.  **Contact Form:** Implement the API endpoint and email-sending logic for the contact form.\\\\n4.  Remove the `announcements` table and related APIs from your plan, as this is superseded by Sanity.\\\\n\\\\nI approve your choice of Fastify, Prisma, and PostgreSQL. Begin recruiting your team and scaffolding the application, starting with the authentication module. Report back with a revised, high-level plan and your recruitment needs.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"BE-PLAN-02\\\"\\n}\\n###<BE-PLAN-02>###\\n###<FE-PLAN-02>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Jung, your frontend plan is outstanding and aligns perfectly with the overall strategy. It is approved. \\\\n\\\\nYour next actions are:\\\\n1.  Begin recruiting your team of supervisors and attendants to handle the component and page development.\\\\n2.  Coordinate with Director Lagret (Ops) to get access to the Next.js/Vercel project and the Sanity.io API keys.\\\\n3.  Coordinate with Director Lystra (Backend) to finalize the API contract for authentication (`/api/auth/*`) and for fetching the list of protected documents (`/api/v1/documents`).\\\\n4.  You are cleared to begin scaffolding the frontend application structure as outlined in your report. Focus first on the global layout, UI component library, and the public pages ('Contact Us', 'Bylaws', 'Schools').\\\\n\\\\nReport back with your recruitment plan and initial project structure.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"FE-PLAN-02\\\"\\n}\\n###<FE-PLAN-02>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAgent response contains multiple call types: STORE, ORDER. Only one call type is allowed per response.\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753468435412,"endTime":1753468472706.7344}